        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(pairing): preserve authorized senders when allowFrom reads fail",
        "body": "Related: #98313\n\nSupersedes #98313 with clean maintainer-owned ancestry from a verified-green `main` SHA. The original diagnosis and canonical-reader fix are by @yetval; Yuval's commit is preserved as the first patch in this branch, and each maintainer refinement retains co-author credit.\n\nAI-assisted: implementation and validation were completed with Codex.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators using `/allowlist` or approving a pairing code could silently lose every existing authorized sender when the account's `allowFrom` store was present but unreadable. A failed pairing approval could also consume the pending code, forcing the sender to pair again after permissions were repaired.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMutation pre-reads now use the canonical allowFrom reader with a fresh-read, fail-closed policy while retaining ordinary cached enforcement reads and existing malformed-JSON behavior. Read and normalization failures abort before the atomic rewrite, and pairing approval removes the pending request only after the idempotent allowFrom grant succeeds.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUnreadable or non-normalizable authorization stores are left byte-identical instead of being rebuilt from an empty fallback. Existing authorized senders remain intact, missing stores still support first-time pairing, account isolation and adapter normalization are unchanged, and failed pairing approvals remain retryable after the underlying store problem is repaired.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Publication base: verified-green `main` SHA `aae1189d90f15a2a1b9cd96fbd629c8d60d1ae04`; CI run 28507984536 settled 108 jobs with zero failures.\n- Exact replay sanity: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/pairing/pairing-store.test.ts src/pairing/allow-from-store-file.test.ts` -> 2 files, 18 tests passed.\n- Formatting: `oxfmt --check` passed for all three changed files; `git diff --check` is clean.\n- Linux permission proof: Testbox `tbx_01kwecmezcwqy28x44yqqkykz8` exercised the real `/allowlist` and `approveChannelPairingCode` mutation paths with a root-owned `0600` store; both raised `EACCES` and preserved the seeded authorization bytes and entries.\n- Broader changed checks on the reviewed patch: Testbox `tbx_01kwecsr9kwptmdt4ehnn8q8nx` passed.\n- Fresh ancestry-clean autoreview: bundled `codex-cli 0.143.0-alpha.26`, `gpt-5.6-sol`, `xhigh`; zero findings, correctness 0.97.\n- Bounded change: only `src/pairing/allow-from-store-file.ts`, `src/pairing/pairing-store.ts`, and `src/pairing/pairing-store.test.ts` differ from the leased base.\n\nNo `CHANGELOG.md` edit.\n",
        "branch": "codex/fix-allowfrom-fail-closed-mutation",
